{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing","kind":"proposition","title":"$S(q) = \\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta(q)/E_0(q)$ vanishes at the classical point $q = 1$ — the SDP-constraint scalar is not the $c_k$ ladder normalization","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-neutron-qvalue-symbolic","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-beta-decay-energy-scale","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/wenzl1988"],"tags":["q-beta","markov-trace","frobenius","diagnostic","ladder-normalization","classical-limit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QBeta.OverE0ClassicalVanishing.qbeta_over_e0_numerator_at_one_eq_zero","text":"q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing.md","leanSource":"q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta(q)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_0^{(N{=}0)}(q)</code> be the substrate closed forms from <a href=\"../nuclear-interactions/neutron-qvalue-symbolic.md\">Symbolic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q</code>-value of free neutron decay</a> and <a href=\"../nuclear-interactions/beta-decay-energy-scale.md\">Energy scale of the Hecke normal form: from dimensionless debt to MeV</a>:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta(q) \\;=\\; m_e \\cdot \\frac{(2q + 1 - q^2)(q+1)}{2q^3},\n\\qquad\nE_0^{(N=0)}(q) \\;=\\; \\frac{m_e}{q(q-1)}.</code></pre>\n<p><em>The ratio</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">S(q) \\;\\coloneqq\\; \\frac{\\mathfrak{Q}_\\beta(q)}{E_0^{(N{=}0)}(q)} \\;=\\; \\frac{(2q + 1 - q^2)\\,(q^2 - 1)}{2 q^2}</code></pre>\n<p><em>satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S(q = 1) = 0</code> as an algebraic identity over any commutative ring.</em></p>\n<p>What this means for the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_k</code> ladder, with the values at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>, is recorded in <a href=\"#rem:q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing-ladder-reading\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-algebraic-qbeta-formalize-first-gates\">the ladder reading</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.9.2","page":"b/prop-q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing","qa":{"counts":{"pass":86,"fail":1,"warn":3,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":75},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Nuclear.QBeta.OverE0ClassicalVanishing.qbeta_over_e0_numerator_at_one_eq_zero","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-over-e0-classical-vanishing.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
